  "narrative_text": "Nine metabolites from a metabolomics study were reconciled across namespaces (all ChEBI IDs confirmed; all InChIKeys distinct and structurally non-conflicting). Three pathway-analysis paradigms were applied: RaMP multi-DB ORA, MetaboAnalystR KEGG PSEA, and FELLA random-walk-with-restart on the KEGG hierarchical graph. All three returned empty result sets (n_input=0 resolved; pathways=[]), indicating that the tools could not map the provided KEGG C-IDs or derived InChIKeys to any entries in their current internal databases. The mummichog m/z-direct wrapper was additionally invoked and returned a ranked pathway list (119 tested) with p-values assigned by permutation resampling, but all pathway overlap_size values were zero (no input compound mapped to any empirical compound in the human_mfn reference network), resulting in an exit-code-1 error. A final attempt to invoke the Reactome ORA wrapper (run_sspa_ora) failed with a ModuleNotFoundError. The systematic failure of enrichment across four independent tools — covering ORA, graph-diffusion, and m/z-direct paradigms — indicates either (a) a database-coverage gap for the specific input identifiers in the current tool versions, or (b) a systematic ID-resolution problem between the KEGG-formatted input (C01074, C00109, etc.) and the internal reference stores. Despite this, the input compounds themselves are chemically coherent and biologically plausible: arachidonic acid, its 5-HETE and 15-HETE hydroxylation products, and leukotriene A4 form a recognizable arachidonate-metabolite sub-network; 2-oxobutanoate and glycerol sit at the intersection of glycolysis and amino-acid catabolism; N-acetylgalactosamine belongs to amino-sugar metabolism; 4-hydroxybenzoate participates in benzoate degradation and ubiquinone biosynthesis. The absence of cross-paradigm enrichment consensus prevents the assignment of a definitive pathway winner, and no driver-metabolite claims can be made with tool-verified support. Limitations: All pathway-enrichment tools failed to return results; cross-paradigm consensus could not be established; no pathway memberships were verified via query_pathway_members; claims are limited to ID reconciliation and compound-class assignments.",
